      "id": "sol.ahsme-1953-p36.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Divisibility by \\(x-3\\) requires \\[ 4(3)^2-6(3)+m=0, \\] so \\(18+m=0\\) and \\(m=-18.\\) Of the listed numbers, only \\(36\\) is an exact multiple of \\(-18.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the factor theorem at \\(x=3\\)",
        "After finding \\(m,\\) test which listed number is divisible by it"
